189
00:09:34.085 --> 00:09:36.965
Amdahl's law and the Universal Scalability Law.

190
00:09:37.245 --> 00:09:38.248
Amdahl's law.

191
00:09:38.528 --> 00:09:43.755
If a fraction s of the work is serial, speed-up with N workers is capped at 1 per second:

192
00:09:45.105 --> 00:09:46.086
The formula:

193
00:09:46.366 --> 00:09:52.659
S(N) = (N) / (1 + s(N-1)) lim Ntoinfty S(N) = (1) / (s).

194
00:09:54.009 --> 00:09:56.185
Universal Scalability Law (Gunther).

195
00:09:56.465 --> 00:10:03.505
It adds a coherency term for the cost of keeping workers consistent with each other, which grows with the number of pairs:

196
00:10:04.855 --> 00:10:05.837
The formula:

197
00:10:06.117 --> 00:10:10.554
C(N) = (N) / (1 + sigma(N-1) + kappa N(N-1)).

