What L1 shows: a 5 % serial fraction caps you at 20 times no matter how many workers you add.

839
00:42:41.745 --> 00:42:47.313
Any coherency cost (κ 0) creates a peak, and past it more pods mean less throughput.

840
00:42:47.593 --> 00:42:56.767
Seven load-test points are enough to recover σ and κ within a few percent and predict the peak, before an HPA finds it for you in production.

841
00:42:57.047 --> 00:43:02.999
Reducing κ (removing all-pod broadcasts) moves the peak further than any amount of hardware.

