1088
01:02:34.351 --> 01:02:37.125
ADR-035 or 036:

1089
01:02:37.405 --> 01:02:41.970
City-partitioned Redis carts; scaling limits from budgets and the USL.

1090
01:02:42.250 --> 01:02:43.167
Context.

1091
01:02:43.447 --> 01:02:46.605
Adding pods reduced throughput (§1.1).

1092
01:02:46.885 --> 01:02:51.898
Carts in sessions needed stickiness, couldn't be merged atomically, and couldn't be partitioned.

1093
01:02:53.248 --> 01:02:54.123
Decision.

1094
01:02:54.403 --> 01:03:01.656
(1) Pods are stateless: identity from the gateway JWT, and guests hold server-signed guest cart ids.

1095
01:03:01.936 --> 01:03:10.363
(2) Carts are Redis HASHes under a city hash tag, mutated only through Lua scripts (set quantity with limits, exactly-once merge).

1096
01:03:10.643 --> 01:03:16.552
A snapshot job keeps a recoverable copy in PostgreSQL using 2 connections per pod.

1097
01:03:16.832 --> 01:03:21.909
(3) Cities map to shards through a versioned shard map, and big cities get their own shard.

1098
01:03:22.189 --> 01:03:28.867
Cities move online with the fence + lazy move + sweeper protocol, and every write script honours the fence.

1099
01:03:29.147 --> 01:03:33.883
(4) Scheduled jobs run under a token-owned lease lock and are idempotent.

1100
01:03:34.163 --> 01:03:45.704
(5) maxReplicas = min(connection budget ÷ pool, USL N ÷ 2), recomputed after every load test and enforced at startup and in CI.

1101
01:03:45.984 --> 01:03:50.336
Per-request global locks and all-pod broadcasts are banned on hot paths.

1102
01:03:51.686 --> 01:03:52.710
Consequences.

1103
01:03:52.990 --> 01:03:57.449
(+) Cart capacity grows by adding shards, not by hoping pods scale.

1104
01:03:57.729 --> 01:04:00.225
(+) A Redis incident affects one city.

1105
01:04:00.505 --> 01:04:02.361
(+) Moves need no downtime.

1106
01:04:02.641 --> 01:04:06.246
(minus ) A shard map service and a move runbook to operate.

1107
01:04:06.526 --> 01:04:15.230
(minus ) Guest and customer carts are per city (a customer who switches cities sees that city's cart, which matches per-city stock and prices).

1108
01:04:15.510 --> 01:04:17.857
(minus ) The accepted anomaly above.

1109
01:04:18.137 --> 01:04:30.403
Revisit when: a single city outgrows one shard (split by zone within the city, the same protocol at finer grain), or cells per region (Ch 34) replace per-service partitioning.

